~ start
Brian: Ehm... Good day? Sir...
Jan: Good day, young lad, how can I help you? We don't get many visitors in this house...
(Should I be truthful... what if this is his house...)

- (Tell the truth)
	Brian: I am searching for my friends. Margaret, Alice, Dan... We wanted to explore this house...
	Brian: We thought it was abandoned...
	Jan: It is. I am just temporarily staying. It needs more furniture.
	Jan: I think I heard someone is in the mirror room.
	Jan: And if you're here for long, the Hallway is most likely.
	Jan: Although I would avoid it if I were you. It is not easy to leave.

- (Lie)
	Brian: I accidentally wandered in here. Can you tell me how to leave?
	Jonáš: Try the nearest door. If you are lucky, it will lead where you need.
	Brian: And if I am not?
	Jonáš: They will lead where the House pleases.
	do SignalManager.fear.emit(5)

=> END

~ start2

Brian: Can I ask, who are you and why are you here?
Ivan: Sure, even though I am not sure how useful it will be. I am Ivan, a traveling carpenter.
Ivan: I travel, make furniture, give it away.
Ivan: I would say I am one of the more skilled ones.
Ivan: I came to this house recently. I wanted to rest a bit.
Ivan: I saw it lacks furniture.
Ivan: I am not used to making furniture per request.
Ivan: But what wouldn't I do for a colleague?

- This house is your colleague?
	John: In a certain sense, yes.
	Brian: How? Why would you think that?
	John: I can tell.
	Brian: I do not understand... it makes no sense.
	John: If you are looking for things that "make sense" in this house,
	John: I fear you will not like what you find.
	do SignalManager.fear.emit(5)

- And where are you going to after you leave this house?
	Jonathan: To Prague. It is a beautiful city. Full of narrow streets.
	Brian:  And what there? You know someone there?
	Jonathan: No. I have work to do.
	Brian: Carpentry?
	Jonathan: Yes, making furniture.
	Jonathan: If you want, and if you leave from here, take a walk through the city.
	Jonathan: And if you see a table or chair on the sidewalk that seems like there is more to it,
	Jonathan: You may take it. Take it as a gift from your old pal, Jonathan.
	Brian: Who is Jonathan?
	Jonathan: Me, of course. I just introduced myself...
	Brian: But...
	Brian: (Didn't he introduce himself... I should go... I have a bad feeling about this.)
	do SignalManager.fear.emit(5)

=> END